<suzuki><manual>
<section sectnbr = "1F">
<servcat sctnbr = "01" scnbr = "06">
<configtype typenbr = "2">
<servinfotype sitcode = "6">
<servinfo servinfosgmlid = "AENLSB0A1626008" svcinfotypenbr = "08" svcinfoqualnbr = "03" page = "2" supplyoff = "1" modify = "0">
<title>
Thermostat Heater Inspection
</title>
<ptxt>
<intxrefpoff refid = "AENLSB0A1626007">Thermostat Heater Removal and Installation:K14D</intxrefpoff>
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Without electric current, thermostat with heater opens in heated water at around boiling temperature under atmospheric pressure. Therefore, check the thermostat heater in coolant to avoid the boiling.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Immerse thermostat heater incorporating heater in coolant and check operation as follows.
</ptxt>
</item>
<list2 type = "ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Leaving connector above coolant, immerse movable valve part of thermostat heater (1) in coolant as shown, and heat coolant gradually.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that wax pellet starts to open at specific temperature.
</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>
Temperature at which valve starts to open (lift 0.35 mm (0.014 in.))
</title>
<ptxt>
95.5 – 98.5 &#176;C (203.9 – 209.3 &#176;F)
</ptxt>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>
Temperature at which valve becomes fully open
</title>
<ptxt>
110 &#176;C (230 &#176;F)
</ptxt>
</spec>
<spec>
<title>
Valve lift
</title>
<ptxt>
More than 8 mm (0.31 in.) at 110 &#176;C (230 &#176;F)
</ptxt>
</spec>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IGJA0A162004.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "86.008mm" ver = "01" gw = "142" gh = "227"/>
<callout>
<table frame = "all" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<tgroup cols = "4" colsep = "1" rowsep = "1">
<colspec colnum = "1" colname = "1" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "2" colname = "2" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<colspec colnum = "3" colname = "3" colwidth = "0.315in"/>
<colspec colnum = "4" colname = "4" colwidth = "1.378in"/>
<tbody>
<row rowsep = "0">
<entry colname = "1" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
2.
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "2" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Thermometer
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "3" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "1" border-right = "0" align = "right">
<ptxt>
3.
</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname = "4" border-top = "1" border-bottom = "1" border-left = "0" border-right = "1" align = "left">
<ptxt>
Heater
</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</callout>
</figure>
</item>
</list2>
<item>
<ptxt>
Using ohmmeter, measure resistance between terminals “1” and “2” at thermostat heater.
</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>
Thermostat heater resistance
</title>
<ptxt>
11 – 15 &#937; at 23 &#176;C (73.4 &#176;F)
</ptxt>
</spec>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname = "IFRA0B162013.swf" width = "88.000mm" height = "61.684mm" ver = "01" gw = "162" gh = "158"/>
</figure>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
If check result is not as specified, replace thermostat heater. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A1626007"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</servinfo>
